rs in respect of, obligations referred to in (ii) above. In the event of incomplete payment of creditors ranking senior to holders of the Notes Disqualified as Tier 1 Own Funds but Qualified as Tier 3 Own Funds (in the context of voluntary or judicial liquidation of the Issuer, bankruptcy proceedings or any othe r similar proceedings affecting the Issuer) the obligations of the Issuer in connection with the Notes Disqualified as Tier 1 Own Funds but Qualified as Tier 3 Own Funds and relative interest will be terminated. 3. Should the Notes no longer be treated as own funds regulatory capital (“Notes Disqualified as Own Funds”), and for so long as they constitute Notes Disqualified as Own Funds, they will cease to constitute deeply subordinated obligations of the Issuer, and will automatically constitute: − before the Existing Subordinated Notes Redemption Date, Unsubordinated Obligations; and − from (and including) the Existing Subordinated Notes Redemption Date, 1 st ranking senior subordinated notes, in each case without the need for any action from the Issuer and without consultation of the Noteholders. The 1st ranking senior subordinated notes rank and shall at all times rank: (i) pari passu without any preference among themselves and (save for certain obligations required to be preferred by French law) equally and rateably with any other existing or future 1st ranking senior subordinated notes; (ii) senior to all present and future: (A) Equity Securities; (B) deeply subordinated obligations; (C) prêts participatifs granted to, and titres participatifs issued by, the Issuer; (D) ordinary subordinated obligations; (E) senior subordinated obligations; and (iii) junior to all present and future: (A) subordinated obligations preferred by mandatory and/or overriding provisions of law; (B) subordinated obligations of the Issuer that rank or are expressed to rank senior to the 1 st ranking senior subordinated notes; and (C) Unsubordinated Obligations. If any judgment is rendered by any competent court declaring the judicial liquidation ( liquidation judiciaire) or, following an order of redressement judiciaire, the sale of the whole business ( cession totale de l’entreprise ) of the Issuer, or if the Issuer is liquidated for any reason, the rights of the Noteholders in respect of principal and interest of the Notes Disqualified as Own Funds will be subordinated to the payments of claims of other creditors of the Issuer includ ing insurance companies and entities referred to in article R.322-132 of the French Code des assurances reinsured by the Issuer, EMEA 149441201 58 holders of insurance policies issued by such entities and creditors with respect to obligations referred to in (iii) above, but will be paid in priority to any holders of, or creditors in respect of, obligations referred to in (ii) above. In the event of incomplete payment of creditors ranking senior to holders of the Notes Disqualified as Own Funds (in the context of voluntary or judicial liquidation of the Issuer, bankruptcy proceedings or any other similar proceedings affecting the Issuer) the obligations of the Issuer in connection with the Notes Disqualified as Own Funds and relative interest will be terminated In all cases, if the Notes are no longer treated as own funds regulatory capital prior to the Existing Subordinated Notes Redemption Date but they are still outstanding on the Existing Subordinated Notes Redemption Date, then they will constitute 1 st ranking senior subordinated notes as from the Existing Subordinated Notes Redemption Date. Pursuant to article L.327-2 of the French Code des assurances, a lien (privilège) over the movable assets of the Issuer is granted for the benefit of the Issuer’s policyholders. Noteholders, even if they are policyholders of the Issuer, do not have the benefit of such lien in relation to amounts due under the Notes. 4. NEGATIVE PLEDGE There will be no negative pledge in respect of the Notes. 5. INTEREST 5.1 Rate of 