h individuals (including car insurance, property insurance, personal accident insurance, school insurance, legal expenses insurance) and professionals. In 2017, SOGECAP became the majority shareholder of Antarius, the captive personal insurance company of Crédit du Nord retail banking network (merged with Société Générale to become SG from 2023) . This acquisition represented a key step in the progress of the strategy aimed at consolidating the integrated bancassurance model of Société Générale Group. From 2017 to 2019, following Société Générale Group’s strategy to refocus its presence on markets where it already benefits from its critical size, SOGECAP has reduced its international presence by selling some of its subsidiaries in countries where Société Générale decided to sell its retail banking network (including Lebanon, Croatia, Bulgaria, Serbia). In 2022, faced with the outbreak of the war in Ukraine at the beginning of the year, Société Générale Group ceased its banking and insurance activities in Russia. In 2024, Société Générale Group sold its banking network in Morocco as well as the insurance company La Marocaine Vie. In the same year, Sogecap signed an agreement for the sale of its EMEA 149441201 85 Romanian pension fund subsidiary, BRD Fond de Pensii, the completion of which could take place by the third quarter of 2025. As of the date of this Information Memorandum, the Group has an international presence in seven countries. During the last few years, in addition to its integrated bancassurance strategy, the Group has accelerated the development of external partnerships to diversify its distribution network and increase growth drivers. In particular, the Group can rely on Oradéa Vie, its life insurance subsidiary fully dedicated to external partnerships in France, which develops innovative products and services mainly delivered through independent financial advisers and private banks. At year -end 2024, Oradéa Vie had outstandings of EUR 9.0 billion (with 56% of outstandings in unit -linked funds), up 9% compared to year-end 2023. With respect to non-life insurance, Sogessur has become one of the top ten car fleet insurers in France. 6. BUSINESS OF THE GROUP 6.1 Geographic Presence Within the Group, four entities are based in France: SOGECAP, Sogessur, Oradéa Vie and Antarius. The Group is also present in six countries outside France through branches (Italy, Germany, Poland, Romania) or subsidiaries (Luxembourg, Czech Republic, Romania). About 3,000 employees work for the Group worldwide, including 700 employees outside of France. SOGECAP and its subsidiaries have been well ranked in the markets in which they operate. In 2024, SOGECAP was the 4th life insurer in France, Komercni Pojistovna the 3rd life insurer in the Czech Republic, BRD Asigurari de Viata the 4th life insurer in Romania and Sogelife the 6th life insurer in Luxembourg. 6.2 Overview – Key figures of the Group (in French GAAP) As of 31 December 202 4, the total consolidated gross revenues of the Group reached EUR 20.4 billion, an increase of 37% compared to 2023. This significant increase, resulting from the growth of all activities, was mainly driven by life insurance savings business (+42% compared to 2023). The rates offered in 2023 on the euro funds and the attractive deposit offers available for 2024 in a favorable market environment are the main contributors to this growth. In the protection business (personal protection and property and casualty insurance), the level of premiums is stable to EUR 2.0 billion in 202 4, supported by the development of the prope rty and casualty insurance business. The net results after tax amounted to EUR 403 million as of 31 December 2024. In 2024, the Group continued to maintain a high level of financial strength with a Solvency II ratio of 191%. The Group continued to offer a competitive performance for its savings life insurance clients, well above the French market average, with a stable average profit-shar